description:
Measured at 1120x740 (the default window): page content 1430 px in a 652 px viewport. Card offsets: master monitor (waveform + transport + export) y=163, FX rack y=505, clip list y=1084 - so the clip list is two screens down, and while adjusting the rack the play/export transport is already 400+ px above the viewport.

The current order is Monitor -> History -> FX rack -> Clips, i.e. the read-only summary is first and the material being edited is last. The workflow the tab documents ('open a take, polish it, reorder/re-generate segments, listen, export') reads better as:
  1. a sticky/fixed transport dock (waveform + play/pause + timecode + export) that stays visible while the body scrolls;
  2. the clip list directly under it (the thing you edit most, and the thing that tells you what the take contains);
  3. the FX rack as compact parameter rows (gain/speed/gap/fades) with the pending-vs-applied state visible;
  4. the op-stack history as a compact, clickable chain (revert-to-step, not only pop-last) at the bottom.

Related consolidation: duration is printed 4x (page header badge, monitor card badge, timecode, waveform labels) and clip count 2x (header + clip card badge); the monitor card's 'Dinh dang xuat: WAV' describes the settings default, not what the save dialog will actually write. Decide one home for each number.

This issue is the umbrella for the layout redesign; the concrete defects are 3cl.1 (sliders), 3cl.2 (idle waveform), 3cl.6 (nested scroll). Acceptance: at 1120x740 the transport and the clip list are both reachable without scrolling past the other; at 640x420 no control collapses or overlaps; no number is printed twice on one screen.
